  "step_3": "The decision reason requires consideration of skewness — specifically, the greater weight on unfavorable outcomes (zero) — and a preference for the more right-skewed lottery. However, the individual’s verbal report focuses exclusively on the probability of winning (positive outcome), not on the probability of losing or the imbalance in the distribution. There is no mention of the 80% vs. 75% chance of zero, nor any reference to skewness or right-skewness. Therefore, the individual did not consider the relevant information for the decision reason. Additionally, the justification provided (focus on winning probability) contradicts the rule of the decision reason, which would prefer the more right-skewed (i.e., more likely to lose) lottery. Since the individual neither considered the skewness nor applied the rule of preferring greater right-skewness, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
